//! `jackioh_cards`: the card registry (BUILD M4-T2, SPEC §10.9, SURFACE §7): every card script file
//! plus `catalog.json`, turned into what the engine, the tests, the validator and the client consume.
//! Port of `packages/cards/src/index.ts` and `catalog-data.ts`. Written once by part 1.
//!
//! - `scripts::<set>::<file>` and `REGISTRY`: generated by `build.rs` from `src/scripts/**` (SURFACE
//!   §7.4), which also proves what `buildRegistry` threw on (a file's `ID` names a real catalog card,
//!   no two files claim one) and what `missing-tests.ts` listed (a catalog id with no file).
//! - `register_all()`: hands the catalog, its code blocks (R1183004), its card metrics (R1846000) and
//!   every card's scripts to the engine, once.
//! - `catalog_json()`, `flavour_json()`, `chinese_json()`, `chinese_terms_json()`, `catalog_version()`:
//!   the data, compiled in (SURFACE §3: data reaches a pure crate only at compile time). The flavour
//!   and Chinese sidecars are generated from `card-text.yaml` (#2498), which no pure crate parses.
//! - `CATALOG`, `CATALOG_IDS`, `CATALOG_VERSION`, `card_def`, `card_def_by_index`: `catalog-data.ts`'s
//!   readers of the shipped catalog, under their TS names (SURFACE §4.2).
//! - `census`: each set's cards, tokens, rarities and tag counts, written once (#2581).
//!
//! The engine gets the WHOLE catalog and only the scripts that exist. A catalog id with no script is
//! a playable card with no text: `scripts::script_of` falls back to an empty script, so a missing card
//! file can never crash a game or a test — it just does nothing.
//!
//! Not ported: `buildRegistry`/`CARDS`/`CardModule` (the registry is generated), and `flavour.ts`
//! (the client's: `apps/web/src/cards/flavour.ts`, part 21).

